eeks, peaking at $98.58 and pulling back 23% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Dec 11, 2025 it closed at $99.42, its first close above the base high of $98.30. Volume that day was 11.6M shares, 1.42x the prior 10-day average of 8.1M. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $131.95, and the chart ends at $112.85.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}